	<ROOT xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="TableInfo.xsd">
		<TABLE Name="StateMachineTable">
			<VIEW Name="STATE_MACHINE_TABLE" Type="File,Database,DatabaseTest" Description="%3Cb%3EState%20Machines%3C%2Fb%3E%20have%20unique%20run%20display%20aliases%20and%20independent%20run%20number%20sequences.%20They%20also%20have%20an%20associated%20system%20alias%20filter%20which%20forces%20users%20to%20only%20consider%20a%20subset%20of%20existing%20system%20aliases%20when%20configuring.%20The%20concept%20of%20the%20%3Cb%3EState%20Machine%3C%2Fb%3E%20selection%20is%20to%20differentiate%20modes%20of%20operation%20for%20a%20set%20of%20state%20machine%20transitions%20(e.g.%20Calibration%20mode%20or%20Physics%20mode).%0A%0AThe%20%3Cb%3EActive%20State%20Machine%3C%2Fb%3E%20can%20be%20selected%2C%20by%20UID%2C%20in%20the%20State%20Machine%20driving%20web%20apps%20(either%20as%20a%20GET%20parameter%20in%20the%20URL%20of%20the%20page%2C%20or%20dynamically%20in%20selection%20boxes%20in%20the%20page).%0A%0AFor%20example%2C%20it%20may%20be%20useful%20to%20have%20a%20%22Calibration%22%20state%20machine%20and%20a%20%22Cosmics%22%20state%20machine.%20In%20which%20case%2C%20it%20may%20be%20useful%20to%20consider%20%22Calibration*%22%20and%20%22Cosmic*%22%20system%20aliases%20respectively%2C%20and%20have%20a%20run%20display%20alias%20of%20%22CalRun%22%20and%20%22CosmicsRun%22%20respectively%20(note%20that%20the%20run%20number%20sequence%20for%20the%20two%20types%20of%20runs%20could%20proceed%20independently).">
